---
description: Nested flynn and flynn-host commands use noun:verb colons, not spaces
alwaysApply: true
---

# Colon commands

`flynn` and `flynn-host` register nested verbs as **one token**: `noun:verb`.
Do not add a new space-nested command (`flynn-host volume gc`) as the canonical name.

Add **additional colons only when they make sense** — a real nested noun, not a hyphenated verb.

```text
# good
flynn env:get DATABASE_URL
flynn plugin:list --known
flynn kafka:topics:create events
flynn-host volume:gc
flynn-host plugin:install redis
flynn-host plugin:credentials:set github
flynn-host firewall:peer:add 10.0.0.5
flynn-host log-sink:add syslog syslog://logs.example:514/
flynn-host acme:disable-system-routes
flynn-host plugin:update-all

# bad (canonical form)
flynn env get DATABASE_URL
flynn kafka:topics-create events
flynn-host volume gc
flynn-host plugin install redis
flynn-host plugin:credentials-set github
flynn-host firewall:peer-add 10.0.0.5
flynn-host acme:disable:system:routes
flynn-host plugin:update:all
flynn-host log:sink:add
```

- **Noun + verb** → colon (`plugin:list`, `acme:configure`, `volume:delete`).
- **Nested noun + verb** → extra colon (`plugin:credentials:set`, `firewall:peer:add`, `kafka:topics:create`).
- **Hyphenated multi-word action or noun stays hyphenated** (`acme:disable-system-routes`, `acme:enable-system-routes`, `plugin:update-all`, `runtime-profile:allow-custom`, `docker:set-push-url`, `cluster:migrate-domain`, `log-sink:add`).
- **Standalone verbs stay verbs** (`backup`, `daemon`, `update`, `ps`, `run`).
- Space form is a **permanent alias** (print `flynn-host volume gc is now flynn-host volume:gc`). When a nested noun used to be hyphenated, that hyphen name is also a permanent alias (print `flynn-host plugin:credentials-set is now flynn-host plugin:credentials:set`). Register the colon name; map space and old hyphen forms in `command_alias.go`.
- Root help lists **parent commands only** (one alphabetical list, no grouped subsections). Nested verbs — including plugin actions such as `redis:dump` — appear under `flynn help <parent>` / `flynn <parent> --help` (and the same for `flynn-host`).
- Docs, errors, and new tests use the colon form. Plugin `plugin:route <name>` is the colon spelling of `plugin <name> route`. Two-token plugin actions are `kafka:topics:create`, not `kafka:topics-create`.
